# Q4 first failing probe — cross-composite reaction.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The simplest expression of the Q4 problem: two sibling sub-composites
# `alice` and `bob`, each holding a single-qubit state. We WANT a
# reaction at the Lab level that ENTANGLES them — CNOT on qubits in
# different composites.
#
# Full vision: reactor detects the cross-composite redex, emits a
# MERGE intent (see `docs/merge-protocol.md`); the merge fuses
# alice+bob into one composite holding their tensor-product state;
# the reaction's reactum applies CNOT inside the merged composite.
#
# THIS FILE PROBES three concrete blockers:
#   1. Composite-output leak (sub-composite outputs include schema
#      descriptors + nested specs, not just slot values)
#   2. `Schema::Any` + `overwrite` doesn't replace (accumulates)
#   3. No sibling-addressing syntax for cross-composite refs
#
# Using `map[float]` instead of `any` (per user's principled-types
# correction) — typed slots, no `any` escape hatch.
#
# Run: `chrysalis run quantum-cross-cnot.ys --time 1`

# A minimal `QuantumSystem` composite — holds a typed state on its bridge.
# `state0` is a PARAM (initial value at instantiation); `state` is a
# typed `map[float]` (bitstring → amplitude). Includes a no-op `Hold`
# process so the composite has SOMETHING active (engine may require
# at least one process for bridge taps to fire).
process Hold ~{state :: map[float]} ->{state :: overwrite[map[float]]}
(
  {state: state}
)

composite QuantumSystem[state0 :: map[float] = {'0': 1.0, '1': 0.0}]
  ~{state :: map[float] @ state = state0}
  ->{state :: map[float] @ state}
(
  state: state0 |
  hold:  Hold ~{state: state} ->{state: state}
)

# A probe step that tries to READ alice's and bob's states by name
# from the parent. If sibling-addressing worked, this would write
# their states into the `seen` slot. (BLOCKER 3 surfaces here — there's
# no path syntax to reach into a sibling composite's bridged slots.)
step Probe
  ~{alice_state :: map[float], bob_state :: map[float]}
  ->{seen :: overwrite[any]}
(
  {seen: {alice: alice_state, bob: bob_state}}
)

# Sibling composites at the same level (no map wrapper). Each
# QuantumSystem writes its bridge `state` to a parent slot
# (`alice_state` / `bob_state`).
composite Lab ~{} ->{
  alice_state :: map[float] @ alice_state,
  bob_state   :: map[float] @ bob_state,
  seen        :: any @ seen
} (
  alice_state: {} |
  bob_state:   {} |
  seen:        {} |
  alice: QuantumSystem[state0: {'0': 0.7071, '1': 0.7071}]
    ~{} ->{state: alice_state} |
  bob:   QuantumSystem[state0: {'0': 1.0, '1': 0.0}]
    ~{} ->{state: bob_state} |
  probe: Probe
    ~{alice_state: alice_state, bob_state: bob_state}
    ->{seen: seen}
)

# The reaction we WANT to express (still commented out — needs the
# probe path to work first as proof-of-concept for sibling reads):
#
# reaction Entangle =
#   alice ~{state: a} | bob ~{state: b}
#   ->
#   merged ~{state: cnot(tensor(a, b))}
